# Marketplace recipe: permission-normaliser exceptions
# (slice 6B flag 1). Read by the app container's init after
# its uniform pass, and applied by onionhost-recipe itself
# after an apply; format:
#   <octal mode> <path relative to the app-data volume>
# marketplace.key is the instance's master key (it keys buyer
# tokens and encrypts stored secrets): the application
# creates it at mode 0600 and it must stay that way - the
# uniform pass would leave it group-readable at 0664. The
# first-boot env copy holds the administrator password in
# plaintext for the one boot it exists in; it is shredded by
# the first-boot step itself, and pinned restrictive here
# for the hours it may wait for a publish retry.
0600 native/marketplace.key
0400 native/.recipe-admin.env
# The recipe's own executables. The uniform pass flattens
# every file to 0664; the golden init re-chmods only the
# archive binary (native/app) before exec, because it is the
# one binary the platform contract knows about. The
# media-worker is exec'd directly by the application (no
# shell), and first-boot.sh / migrate.sh are declared 0755
# in the manifest - all three keep their mode here. (Found
# in the recipe's sandbox venue: without the media-worker
# pin, image uploads failed with "Media worker error"
# because the worker binary had lost its exec bit.)
0755 native/media-worker
0755 native/first-boot.sh
0755 native/migrate.sh
